  "entry": "code/app.py",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Load an EEG recording (the synthetic demo, a CSV or an EDF), look at the per-channel waveforms and spectrum, flag flat, clipped, high-amplitude and missing data over 1-second windows using thresholds you can change, and export an HTML report and a CSV metrics table, all on your own machine and without making any diagnostic claims. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
